1335,"**React Aria integration**: Built on React Aria Select for accessibility, keyboard navigation, and typeahead"],[2115,"**Recommended default**: Use `Flex` for most layouts. Since it extends `Box`, you get all `Box` capabilities without needing to nest components."],[774,"**Reduced DOM Size**: Path data stored once instead of duplicated"],[769,"**Reference Rendering**: Each icon renders as a lightweight `<use>` element that references the sprite"],[1869,"**Responsive behavior**: Auto-sizing with horizontal scrolling for many data points, sticky axes"],[1906,"**Responsive sizing**: `useParentSize` hook provides efficient resize detection with debouncing (15ms)"],[1798,"**Right** — when the group represents utility or contextual controls (e.g. grid/list view toggle)."],[1874,"**RTL support*&#x2A;: Full right-to-left layout support for international audiences &#x2A;(in development)*"],[1904,"**Scales**: VisX's `scaleBand` and `scaleLinear` for efficient coordinate mapping"],[1901,"**Screen reader support**: Semantic HTML structure with proper ARIA attributes"],[1630,"**SegmentedController Container:** `data-disabled`"],[1631,"**SegmentedControllerItem:** `data-selected`, `data-hovered`, `data-pressed`, `data-focus-visible`, `data-disabled`"],[1358,"**Shared structural containers.** These generic, layout-only components are the building blocks for composing a component's interior (a `Modal`, a card, a panel). They are semantic containers built on `Flex`, so they accept the same layout props (`direction`, `gap`, `alignItems`, `justifyContent`, `padding`, ...)."],[431,"**Shift + Tab**: Moves focus to the previous checkbox"],[1935,"**Simplify tooltips**: If tooltips are complex, consider using simpler content or disabling them"],[1867,"**Single and multi-series support**: Display one or multiple data series with grouped bars"],[1330,"**Single or multiple selection**: Set `selectionMode=\"multiple\"` to allow multiple values"],[878,"**Single or multiple selection**: Set `selectionMode=\"single\"` or `\"multiple\"`."],[534,"**Sizes**: Each picker is a `SizeProvider`. `size` (`sm`, `md`, `lg`) sets its label, trigger, description, error, and the calendar it opens; without it, the picker follows the surrounding scope"],[1712,"**Sizes**: The field is a `SizeProvider`. `size` (`sm`, `md`, `lg`) sets its label, input, description, error, and composed controls; without it, the field follows the surrounding scope. An explicit `size` on a part still wins for that part"],[1035,"**Sizes**: The field is a `SizeProvider`. `size` (`sm`, `md`, `lg`) sets its label, input, steppers, description, and error; without it, the field follows the surrounding scope"],[1333,"**Sizes**: The field is a `SizeProvider`. `size` (`sm`, `md`, `lg`) sets the label, trigger, and options, which open at the same size even though they render in a portal. Without it, the Select follows the surrounding scope"],[1775,"**Space / Enter**"],[1220,"**Space**: Select the focused radio button"],[430,"**Space**: Toggles the focused checkbox"],[926,"**Space/Enter**: activate an item; **Escape**: close"],[1634,"**Space/Enter**: Select the focused segment"],[768,"**Sprite Sheet Creation**: A hidden SVG sprite sheet is automatically injected into the DOM containing symbol definitions"],[778,"**SSR Limitation**: Sprite references render empty until client-side hydration"],[1366,"**Standalone** - with no parent context it renders with its own structural defaults and looks the same everywhere."],[1034,"**Steppers**: A stepper is a `Group` holding `Button slot=\"decrement\"`, an `Input`, and `Button slot=\"increment\"`. Left empty, each button takes its icon and `variant=\"control\"` from the field, so no icon imports are needed. Compose a bare `Input` instead for a plain numeric input"],[1909,"**Sticky axes**: Positioned absolutely to remain visible during scroll"],[1898,"**Sticky y-axis**: The y-axis remains visible during horizontal scroll"],[718,"**Styling**: `className`, `style`, `data-*` attributes"],[762,"**SVG Parsing**: The fetched SVG string is parsed into a React element using `@bento/svg-parser`"],[1771,"**Tab**"],[429,"**Tab**: Moves focus to the next/previous checkbox"],[1217,"**Tab**: Moves focus to/from the radio group"],[1632,"**Tab**: Moves focus to/from the segmented controller"],[1677,"**The body is `<Text slot=\"body\">`**, once or as many times as the copy needs."],[1675,"**The eyebrow is `slot=\"eyebrow\"`**, on either a `Text` or a `Tag`. The two forms swap\nfreely, and a `Tag` is sized to pair with the lockup."],[1676,"**The title is `<Heading slot=\"title\">`.** Pick the level from the document outline, not the\nvisual size: `size` handles the visuals, so `level={1}` in an `xs` lockup is perfectly valid."],[1172,"**Titles overflow:** that's expected — titles truncate. Shorten the title."],[1767,"**ToggleButton Item:** `data-selected`, `data-hovered`, `data-pressed`, `data-focus-visible`, `data-disabled`"],[1766,"**ToggleButtonGroup Container:** `data-size`"],[1913,"**Tooltips** use absolute positioning and scroll-aware calculations for accurate placement"],[1902,"**Tooltips**: Show on both hover and focus for keyboard users"],[777,"**Trade-offs:**"],[719,"**Transform**: `rotate`, `flip` for icon transformations"],[533,"**Trigger and calendar**: An empty `Button slot=\"trigger\"` renders a calendar icon and the formatted value from the field. `DatePickerCalendar` (and `DateRangePickerCalendar`) is the calendar in the popover it opens: it takes `Calendar` props plus `popoverProps` for the overlay. Write `Popover`, `Content`, and `Calendar` yourself to replace the whole overlay"],[1328,"**Trigger and options**: An empty `Button slot=\"trigger\"` renders the selected value and a chevron from the field. `SelectOptions` is the list in the popover the Select opens: it takes `ListBox` props (including `items` with a render function for a dynamic collection) plus `popoverProps` for the overlay. Write `Popover`, `Content`, and `ListBox` yourself to replace the whole overlay"],[929,"**Type to select**: jump to a matching item (string labels are used as `textValue`)"],[2089,"**Typed Refs:** Refs are correctly typed based on the `as` value - `useRef<HTMLButtonElement>` works with `as=\"button\"`."],[713,"**TypeScript support**: Fully typed with comprehensive prop interfaces"],[1876,"**TypeScript support**: Fully typed with comprehensive prop interfaces"],[2153,"**Use `Grid` when**: You need explicit two-dimensional layouts with rows and columns, named grid areas, or responsive auto-fill patterns."],[780,"**Use default mode** for SSR applications or when icons appear infrequently"],[781,"**Use sprite mode** when the same icons appear many times (navigation, lists, tables)"],[791,"**Use sprite mode**: For repeated icons, consider sprite mode which consolidates multiple icons into a single SVG sprite sheet, reducing DOM size and improving performance when the same icon appears multiple times"],[1038,"**Validation states**: Use `isInvalid` with a `FieldError` and `isDisabled` for validation and disabled state"],[1332,"**Validation states**: Use `isInvalid` with a `FieldError` and `isDisabled` for validation and disabled state"],[1711,"**Validation states**: Use `isInvalid` with a `FieldError` and `isDisabled` for validation and disabled state"],[1036,"**Value scale**: `minValue`, `maxValue`, `step`, and `formatOptions` configure the numeric behavior"],[1931,"**Verify event targets**: Tooltips use mouse event coordinates and bar group positions"],[1868,"**Vertical and horizontal orientations**: Choose the best layout for your data and use case"],[1907,"**Vertical charts**: Horizontal scrolling when many data points exceed container width"],[1877,"**VisX integration**: Leverages VisX primitives for scales, axes, shapes, and responsive layout"],[767,"**What happens with sprite mode:**"],[1450,"`--color-input-background-default`"],[1447,"`--color-input-background-selected`"],[1456,"`--color-input-text-default`"],[1457,"`--ux-1glcx6s`"],[1445,"`--ux-1m9ys0v`"],[1451,"`--ux-1nu8itt`"],[1454,"`--ux-1sbfig8`"],[1448,"`--ux-sywk25`"],[1460,"`--ux-zvaw3s`"],[206,"`@godaddy/antares/date` re-exports `@internationalized/date`, the package behind these date primitives."],[2132,"`<Box blockAlignChildren=\"center\">`"],[2134,"`<Box inlineAlignChildren=\"center\">`"],[2128,"`<Box orientation=\"horizontal\">`"],[2130,"`<Box orientation=\"vertical\">`"],[2135,"`<Flex alignItems=\"center\">`"],[2131,"`<Flex direction=\"column\" >`"],[2129,"`<Flex direction=\"row\" >`"],[2133,"`<Flex justifyContent=\"center\">`"],[2085,"`2xl` - 2x extra large spacing"],[649,"`acceptedFileTypes` is a best-effort filter for the OS picker — always validate file type and size again in your `onSelect` handler, since it can be bypassed."],[1670,"`align` centers the parts as well as the text, so a `Tag` eyebrow stays centered too."],[1223,"`aria-checked` indicates selection state"],[1637,"`aria-checked` indicates selection state"],[372,"`aria-describedby` wires the `helperText` to the progressbar for screen readers"],[432,"`aria-disabled` for disabled checkboxes"],[1224,"`aria-disabled` for disabled options"],[1638,"`aria-disabled` for disabled segments"],[434,"`aria-invalid` for validation errors"],[1226,"`aria-invalid` for validation errors"],[1783,"`aria-label` (or `aria-labelledby`) is required on the group container"],[1639,"`aria-label` required on the container for screen readers"],[371,"`aria-labelledby` associates the visible label when the `label` prop is provided"],[1124,"`aria-labelledby` associates the visible label when the `label` prop is provided"],[433,"`aria-required` when selection is required"],[1225,"`aria-required` when selection is required"],[369,"`aria-valuemin` and `aria-valuemax` define the range (default `0`–`100`)"],[1122,"`aria-valuemin` and `aria-valuemax` define the range (default `0`–`100`)"],[1121,"`aria-valuenow` is omitted while indeterminate; otherwise it reflects the current value"],[368,"`aria-valuenow` is omitted while indeterminate; otherwise it reflects the current value (clamped to 0–100)"],[1123,"`aria-valuetext` and visible value text are omitted while indeterminate; otherwise `aria-valuetext` provides a formatted string (e.g. `\"60%\"`)"],[370,"`aria-valuetext` and visible value text are omitted while indeterminate; otherwise `aria-valuetext` provides a formatted string (e.g. `\"60%\"`) via `Intl.NumberFormat`; the same string is rendered inside the circle. Override the text with the `aria-valuetext` prop, or control formatting with `formatOptions`"],[2077,"`Box` is a polymorphic layout component that renders as any HTML element or custom component via the `as` prop. It provides consistent spacing, elevation, rounding, and self-alignment within flex or grid containers."],[495,"`Button slot=\"trigger\"` renders a native button with `aria-expanded` for its open state and\n`aria-controls` linked to the panel automatically."],[205,"`Calendar` values are `CalendarDate` objects. Import the date primitives you need from the `@godaddy/antares/date` subpath:"],[252,"`CardSelectionIndicator` only shows a Card's selection state. The `CardGroup` owns selection, so a\nCard stays selectable without an indicator. Pass non-interactive children or a selection-state\nrender function to replace the default circle and icon. See the Multiple selection example."],[1888,"`categoryColors` maps individual category values to palette color indices, overriding\nthe series color for just those bars — so a single series can carry a different color\nper category. All three periods here share the same category-to-color map, so each\nchannel keeps one color across every period; the comparison periods are dropped to\nreduced opacity."],[418,"`CheckboxGroup` is composed: write `Label`, a `Group` holding the `Checkbox` items, `Text slot=\"description\"`, and `FieldError`. The `Group` takes its axis, gap, and presentational role from the group's `orientation`, so a bare `<Group>` is all you need; pass your own `direction`/`gap` to lay the items out differently. Each `Checkbox` takes label text next to the indicator."],[321,"`ChipButton` for menu filters and other actions with a Chip-like appearance"],[339,"`ChipButton` is a real button and exposes menu state through `MenuTrigger`; provide an accessible name when the visible content is incomplete."],[317,"`ChipGroup` + `ChipList` + `Chip` for grouped values, selection, keyboard navigation, and removal"],[332,"`ChipGroup` owns selection and removal behavior. Use a Chip render prop for\nstate-dependent content, and `Button` with `slot=\"remove\"` together with\n`onRemove` for removable items. See **Toggle Chips** and **Removable Chips**."],[1825,"`className` and `style` apply to the tooltip panel."],[486,"`Collapsible`: `data-expanded`, `data-disabled`, and `data-focus-visible-within`."],[496,"`CollapsiblePanel` is labeled by its trigger through `aria-labelledby` automatically."],[497,"`CollapsiblePanel` uses `role=\"group\"` by default. Keep it when the panel's content does not need\na navigation landmark; there is no need to set it explicitly."],[488,"`CollapsiblePanel`: `data-focus-visible-within`."],[2045,"`colorIndex` pins each series to a palette color. Any series can use any index,\nindependently — here two pairs each share an index so an actual line and its\ndashed forecast read as the same color, distinguished only by line style."],[1158,"`currentStep` is the single source of truth for the timeline. Omit it for a not-yet-started flow where every step is `future`; pass the step count for a fully completed flow where every step is `past`."],[742,"`data-color`: Applied when color prop is set"],[745,"`data-flip`: Applied when flip prop is set (\"horizontal\" or \"vertical\")"],[741,"`data-icon`: The icon name (always present)"],[743,"`data-loading`: Applied during icon loading from CDN"],[744,"`data-mode`: Applied when mode prop is set (e.g., \"sprite\")"],[746,"`data-rotate`: Applied when rotate prop is set (90, 180, or 270)"],[1438,"`data-selected`, `data-hovered`, `data-pressed`, `data-focused`, `data-focus-visible`, `data-disabled`, `data-readonly`, `data-invalid`, `data-required`, `data-size`"],[535,"`DatePicker` (single) and `DateRangePicker` (range): a read-only formatted date label; the whole field opens a calendar popover"],[1588,"`Detail` is supporting copy, such as captions and metadata, on the detail ramp. It keeps the\nsurrounding color; add `emphasis=\"passive\"` to mute it."],[569,"`DrawerTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Drawer>`, handling open\nstate automatically."],[663,"`emphasis` picks a feedback color and changes only the color."],[1579,"`emphasis` picks a feedback color and changes only the color."],[1587,"`emphasis` selects a feedback color and changes nothing else. Without it, text inherits the\nsurrounding color."],[1068,"`Enter/Space`"],[60,"`Enter` / `Space`"],[493,"`Enter` / `Space`"],[611,"`Enter` / `Space`"],[857,"`Enter` / `Space`"],[578,"`Escape`"],[994,"`Escape`"],[1070,"`Escape`"],[1830,"`Escape`"],[648,"`FileTrigger` adds no visuals or ARIA of its own — accessibility comes from the pressable child you provide. Use a component with an accessible name (e.g. an Antares `Button` with clear label text) so assistive technology announces the action. The underlying `<input>` is visually hidden but remains operable by keyboard through the child's press behavior."],[2114,"`Flex` is a one-dimensional layout component for arranging children in rows or columns with alignment and spacing control. It extends `Box`, inheriting all `Box` capabilities (padding, elevation, rounding, self-alignment, and polymorphic `as` prop)."],[750,"`focusable=\"false\"`: Prevents keyboard focus"],[2152,"`Grid` is a two-dimensional CSS Grid layout component for complex grid-based layouts. It extends `Box`, inheriting all `Box` capabilities (padding, elevation, rounding, self-alignment, and polymorphic `as` prop)."],[665,"`Heading` renders a semantic `h1`-`h6` element via the `level` prop.\nInside a `Modal`/`Dialog`, add `slot=\"title\"` and it labels the dialog automatically."],[260,"`href` on a standalone Card renders the Card itself as a native link, named by its content unless\nyou pass `aria-label`. A link Card cannot contain controls, so do not put CornerActions, buttons,\nor inputs in it. Inside a `CardGroup`, `href` navigates from the row instead."],[244,"`href` renders the Card itself as a native link, so layered content like an elevated Box stays\nclickable. The link takes its name from its content unless you pass `aria-label`. Do not nest\ncontrols in a link Card."],[500,"`Icon slot=\"indicator\"` is decorative and receives `aria-hidden=\"true\"` automatically."],[845,"`InlineDrawerPanel` is the collapsible content for the accordion pattern — a thin wrapper over RAC `DisclosurePanel` that hides when collapsed. The trigger is any component you slot in with `slot=\"trigger\"` — there's no dedicated trigger component."],[816,"`Input` is the single-line control inside a field, not a field on its own. Prefer `TextField` or `NumberField` as the parent; see those components for fuller examples."],[250,"`isDisabled` fades the Card. A disabled link Card does not navigate, and a disabled Card in a\nCardGroup cannot be selected, run its action, or take focus. `disabledKeys` on the group does\nthe same by key."],[261,"`isDisabled` fades the Card. On a link Card it stops navigation. In a `CardGroup` it also stops\nselection, the action, and focus, as does listing the Card's `id` in `disabledKeys`."],[2028,"`legendPosition` puts the legend above or below the plot, or hides it with `null`. Multi-series charts get a bottom legend by default."],[666,"`level` sets the semantics and `size` sets the look, so the two never have to match. Without\n`size`, a heading takes the size scope's heading tier at any level."],[2083,"`lg` - Large spacing"],[883,"`ListBox` requires either `aria-label` or `aria-labelledby`. For a labeled, popover-style picker, prefer `Select`."],[2082,"`md` - Medium spacing"],[918,"`MenuTrigger` exposes its open state via `isOpen`/`onOpenChange`,\nwhich can be used to drive the rotation of a chevron icon."],[203,"`minValue` / `maxValue` bounds and `isDateUnavailable` per-day disabling"],[538,"`minValue` / `maxValue` bounds and `isDateUnavailable` per-day disabling"],[987,"`Modal` accepts `isOpen` and `onOpenChange` directly, so it can be controlled without a\n`ModalTrigger`. Useful when the modal is opened from several places at once."],[982,"`ModalTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Modal>`, handling open state automatically. Based on RAC `DialogTrigger`."],[1157,"`orientation` switches between `horizontal` (accent bar on top) and `vertical` (accent bar on the leading edge)."],[1880,"`orientation=\"horizontal\"` swaps the axes: categories run down the side and values across the bottom. Reach for it when the labels are long or the chart is really a ranking."],[1507,"`overflowLabels` is optional and defaults to \"Previous tabs\" and \"Next tabs\". Provide localized labels when needed; they should describe the logical direction rather than physical directions like \"left\" or \"right\", as the component automatically handles RTL layouts."],[1820,"`overlay` elevation panel positioned relative to its trigger, with an optional arrow"],[865,"`placement` does not flip in RTL; the side is decided by document/flex order."],[848,"`placement` selects the collapse axis (`left`/`right` → width, `top`/`bottom` → height)"],[1062,"`PopoverTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Popover>`, handling open state and positioning automatically.\nBased on RAC `DialogTrigger`. To anchor a popover to an element it doesn't wrap, pass `triggerRef` instead."],[851,"`prefers-reduced-motion` support"],[1096,"`Pressable` accepts the React Aria press props, including `onPress`, `onPressStart`, `onPressEnd`, `onPressUp`, and `onPressChange`."],[1101,"`Pressable` automatically applies React Aria state attributes such as `[data-hovered]`, `[data-pressed]`, `[data-focus-visible]`, and `[data-disabled]` to the child. Ensure the child component styles these states appropriately if it overrides the default `Pressable` styles."],[1212,"`RadioGroup` is composed: write `Label`, a `Group` holding the `Radio` items, `Text slot=\"description\"`, and `FieldError`. The `Group` takes its axis, gap, and presentational role from the group's `orientation`, so a bare `<Group>` is all you need; pass your own `direction`/`gap` to lay the items out differently. Each `Radio` takes label text next to the indicator. `orientation` also sets keyboard-navigation direction and ARIA."],[2047,"`renderTooltip` example combining a pair of series. Each pair shares a `colorIndex`\n(solid actual + dashed forecast); hovering either line shows the percent change of\nthe forecast against the actual for that pair, wrapped in the default styled popover."],[2048,"`renderTooltip` example styled as a period-over-period comparison card. Paired series\n(solid current period + dashed previous period) share a `colorIndex`; hovering either\nline shows both dated values and the percent change, wrapped in the default popover."],[2046,"`renderTooltip` lets you render a fully custom tooltip and know which curve is\nhovered. Paired series share a `colorIndex`; hovering either line shows a\ntooltip specific to that line, wrapped in the default styled popover."],[996,"`role=\"dialog\"` is applied automatically by the underlying React Aria `Dialog`"],[1072,"`role=\"dialog\"` is applied automatically by the underlying React Aria `Dialog`"],[582,"`role=\"dialog\"` with `aria-modal=\"true\"` on the drawer panel (via RAC Modal)"],[749,"`role=\"img\"`: When title prop is provided"],[748,"`role=\"presentation\"`: For decorative icons"],[367,"`role=\"progressbar\"` on the container"],[1120,"`role=\"progressbar\"` on the container"],[1222,"`role=\"radio\"` on each option"],[1636,"`role=\"radio\"` on each segment"],[1221,"`role=\"radiogroup\"` on the container"],[1635,"`role=\"radiogroup\"` on the container"],[1782,"`selectionMode=\"multiple\"` → `role=\"toolbar\"` on container, `role=\"button\"` + `aria-pressed` per item"],[248,"`selectionMode=\"multiple\"` lets each Card toggle on its own. CardSelectionIndicator shows the\nstate, and its children can render custom content from it. Nested buttons keep their own presses."],[1781,"`selectionMode=\"single\"` → `role=\"radiogroup\"` on container, `role=\"radio\"` + `aria-checked` per item"],[249,"`selectionMode=\"single\"` keeps one Card selected at a time. Arrow keys move between Cards, and\nSpace selects the focused one."],[924,"`size` controls item density. Shown here as two standalone menus so both\nsizes are visible at once; in practice you set `size` on the `Menu` inside a\n`MenuTrigger`."],[1578,"`size` picks a step on the component's own ramp (`xs` to `2xl`) and changes only the font size."],[1668,"`size` sets every part, each on its own role ramp. Without it, the lockup follows the size\nscope."],[1046,"`size` sets the label, input, and steppers. Without it, the field follows the surrounding size\nscope."],[1719,"`size` sets the label, input, description, and any control composed inside. Without it, the\nfield follows the surrounding size scope."],[550,"`size` sets the label, trigger, and calendar. Without it, the picker follows the surrounding\nsize scope."],[988,"`size` sets the modal's text, controls, and spacing. Without it, the modal follows the size\nscope around its trigger."],[664,"`slot=\"title\"` inside a `Modal` or `Dialog` sets the accessible name, and takes the overlay's\ntitle tier, one step above the heading tier."],[2081,"`sm` - Small spacing"],[1383,"`sm`, `md`, or `lg` for the adopted components inside (listed below): their text, controls, and\ndefault spacing."],[95,"`Space` / `Enter`"],[1464,"`Space` toggles the switch when it has focus"],[1159,"`status` is independent of timeline and only controls the status icon and (for `error`) the accent bar color."],[93,"`Tab`"],[580,"`Tab`"],[609,"`Tab`"],[859,"`Tab`"],[992,"`Tab`"],[1828,"`Tab`"],[58,"`Tab` / `Shift + Tab`"],[491,"`Tab` / `Shift + Tab`"],[1511,"`Tab`: `data-selected`, `data-hovered`, `data-pressed`, `data-focus-visible`, and `data-disabled`."],[1508,"`TabList` must be rendered inside `Tabs` and must provide `aria-label` or `aria-labelledby`. Give each `Tab` and its corresponding `TabPanel` the same `id`; React Aria uses that key to build their accessible relationship."],[1512,"`TabPanel`: `data-inert` when a force-mounted inactive panel is not interactive."],[1510,"`Tabs`: `data-design=\"underline\"` or `data-design=\"manilla\"`."],[1576,"`Text` applies the body role and `Detail` the detail role, each at the tier of the nearest\n`SizeProvider`, or `md` outside any scope."],[1575,"`Text` is body copy and `Detail` is supporting copy: captions, metadata, and hints."],[1596,"`TextArea` is the multiline control inside a field, not a field on its own. Prefer `TextField` as the parent; see that component for fuller examples."],[1673,"`TextLockup` positions and type-sets its parts; you supply them. That means anything else can\nsit alongside them — a call to action, a second paragraph, an image — without the component\ngrowing a prop for it."],[1279,"`thumbNames` configures native form field names and does not provide accessible labels. Likewise, `valueLabel`, `minLabel`, and `maxLabel` are visual context rather than substitutes for accessible naming."],[963,"`titleInfo` requires `title` to be set — the info icon is contextually tied to the title label. If `title` is absent, `titleInfo` has no effect."],[1819,"`TooltipTrigger` wraps a focusable element and a `<Tooltip>`, handling hover/focus state and positioning automatically."],[2039,"`tooltipValueFormatter` shapes only the tooltip values, so you can show full currency or units there while the axis stays compact."],[964,"`trend` is intended to accompany `description` to provide temporal context (e.g. \"↑ +3% vs. last month\"). A trend icon alone, with no description, leaves the direction unanchored (\"up since *when*?\"). If `description` is not provided, `trend` has no effect."],[2049,"`variant` sets each series' line style — 'solid' (default), 'dashed', or\n'dotted' — useful for distinguishing actuals from forecasts or targets. The\nlegend swatch mirrors each line's style."],[2027,"`xBaseline` and `yBaseline` control the main axis lines themselves. Dropping them gives a lighter, more editorial chart."],[1882,"`xDomain` and `yDomain` pin down exactly which categories and value range to draw. Here category `F` has no data and still gets an empty slot, and the Y range stays `[0, 40]` even though the largest bar is 30 - handy when several charts need to share a scale."],[2032,"`xDomain` and `yDomain` pin the visible range. Use them to keep a fixed scale, or to keep several charts comparable."],[2023,"`xGridlines` and `yGridlines` add faint lines across the plot so it is easier to read a value back off an axis."],[2084,"`xl` - Extra large spacing"],[2025,"`xLabels` and `yLabels` toggle the tick labels on each axis. Turn them off for sparklines or when the surrounding UI already names the values."],[2033,"`xNice` and `yNice` round the domain out to friendlier numbers (e.g. 0.2 to 1.0), so ticks land on values people expect."],[2036,"`xPaddingOuter` and `yPaddingOuter` add breathing room at the ends of a band or point scale so the first and last values are not pinned to the edges."],[2080,"`xs` - Extra small spacing"],[1883,"`xTickFormat` and `yTickFormat` shape the axis labels - abbreviated dates on one axis, thousands separators on the other. The functions receive the raw accessor value, so they also cover currency, units, or percentages."],[2029,"`xTickFormat` and `yTickFormat` shape the axis labels - dates, currency, units, percentages - and the tooltip follows the same formatting."],[2026